From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:20:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 049/105] R5: GDN projections write mixed_qkv/z/b/a directly,
 dropping the re-layout copy

SGLANG_GDN_PROJ_DIRECT_LAYOUT=1 (default off).

For the contiguous Qwen3.5 checkpoint layout the fused split/reshape/cat kernel
is a pure row compaction: in_proj_qkvz produces [all_q | all_k | all_v | all_z]
and the consumers want [all_q | all_k | all_v] plus z as two separately
row-contiguous tensors; in_proj_ba produces [all_b | all_a] and the consumers
want b and a. No head is reordered, no value changes -- the kernel only exists
because the two halves need their own row strides. That is 36 launches per
verify step (one per GDN layer), ~2.8 us each.

With the flag on, the layer allocates the four consumer buffers up front and
the two projections write them with the two-destination GEMV epilogue: qkvz via
`Fp8LinearMethod.apply_into_split` (new; the W8A16 GEMV path only), b/a via
`bf16_gemv(out=, out2=, split_n=)`. The qkvz/ba parallel-stream structure is
preserved exactly (qkvz on the current stream, ba on alt_stream under the same
capture-mode/threshold condition). Composes with R2: when the backend hands
back stash slices, the ba GEMV writes the stash and no a/b buffer is allocated
at all.

Everything else falls back to the untouched control flow: non-CUDA, aiter,
TP>1, the merged BF16 in_proj weight, a non-fused head-group ratio, a
non-GEMV-able qkvz weight, M>16, or a non-2-D/non-bf16 input.

Bit-exactness on real layer-0 weights (in_proj_qkv/z/a/b of
Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4-mtpft3, per-channel FP8 for qkvz), M=1/4/16: all four
of mixed_qkv, z, b and a are torch.equal to the current
gemv-then-split-kernel result. The GEMV itself is untouched -- same k loop,
same fp32 accumulation order, same per-channel scale index, same bf16 rounding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
